{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790613926,"nonce":"BQu0qsE1VnmkV65Mj/zN7ednjFs=","message":"Rescoped 2026-09-28: no --watch. A loop with backoff is a scheduler inside git-work, and automation is out of scope (483dbe2, AGENTS.md): anything periodic is an external cron calling the CLI. So `git work sync` is one pass, import then export, one write-lock section per entity, polling Jira with JQL `updated \u003e= \u003clast sync\u003e` and honouring rate limits within the pass (Retry-After, bounded retries). Running it every N minutes is a cron entry, which requires the pass to be idempotent and to resume from its own watermark. No webhooks, as before.","files":null}]}